Cars are the most common use of transportation is todays society, but can limiting car usage be beniftial to our citizens? While you read this i want you to think how this can benefit you. Have you ever considered walking over driving, maybe even biking over driving, if not i want you to consider it next time you go to the gym or wherever you go. Limiting our car usage can be done in many types pf ways, such as: walking, biking, or jogging. If we walk instead ov drive not only are we getting to where we need to be, but you also get a workout. Same as jogging and biking, as you can see limiting car usage isnt that bad becasue you can do your body a much needed favor and get some exercise. We all know how we complain about gas prices, so if you cut back on driving you wont have to worry about gas. These are just two of many ways we can limit our car usage.
I think the author supports his idea that studing Venus is a worthy pursuit despite the dangers because he tells why he agree with this but explaing that it isn't that different for Earth and that it used to have Oceans and could have supported like forms. He also explains that it would not be a good idea because it would be 170 degrees Fahrenheit and would won't be able to survive in that heat. He says both sides of the point so they can see where is he doubting this topic. In some places he says that is would be a lot of money and it might not be worth the effort to build things for so many years and not even get to collect data. The things NASA is sending to space to look at Venus is only from a distance, this causes then to not collect as much data so see if humans are ableto live her. I think that if we have the right materials then we should be able to see if life forms like animals and humans can live here. I think that NASA should study it up close even if it takes a lot of money because if we had to option to have two planets then that would be good. This would be good because if anything happens to earth where we need a new planet or it gets destroyed then we could move to Venus and start new life. I agree with the author and think that trying this out would be good for humans as they upgrade each generation.
Venus is a worthy pursuit despite the dangers it presents because as the space program learns more from past experiences, more research can go towards the future and the study of Venus and possibly other planets in our solar system. The human population craves more knowlege. Studying Venus will further our knowlege and help with future development. We learn more by taking risks. The author supports this idea by giving facts on how studying this planet could be beneficial to us. In the text it states "Astronomers are facinated by Venus because it may well have once been the most Earth-like planet in our solar system. Long ago, Venus was probably covered with oceans and could have supported various forms of life, just like Earth." Since Venus was most like Earth we could learn how time changed Venus from possibly being covered in oceans and could have supported life to extreme conditions far from anything humans have encountered. Also in the text it states "Furthermore, recall that Venus can sometimes be our nearest option for a planetary visit, a crucial consideration given the long time frames of space travel." Because the planets in our solar system are very far from Earth it can take a long time for spacecrafts to land and come back if needed to, but since Venus is sometimes ou nearest option for a visit why not give it a chance. Venus is worthy of time and pursuit no matter what danger looms ahead. When we put in the effort to do something we can do anything, already Nasa is developing plans to study Venus further and inventining new inventions to make this happen.
When cell phones were created, it created a huge impact in everyone's lives people would use it for everything like texting, talking, planning, reminders etc. When we have our phones sometimes we do two things at once, but some people multitask at the wrong time like using their phones while driving. We have to start focusing on how much we can do at one time and think about personal safety and the safety of others each time we don't put our phones down. Using a cell phone while driving is dangerous for the driver themselves for many reasons like a car accident can occur when your eyes are off the road. Having your eyes off the road and on your cellular can be terrible for both parties because one party can either lose their life or one party would have to pay damages and get their license suspended because of the dumb decision they made. When driving sometimes it can be diffcult.
